        <updated>2026-06-29T13:13:37.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 149 adds support for responsive iframe sizing; see <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5108373464547328" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5108373464547328</a> (it says 151, but the feature still seems to be behind a pref, since 149).</p>
<p dir="auto">This relies on three new features:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The CSS <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-4/#propdef-frame-sizing" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">frame-sizing</code></a> property</li>
<li>The <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-4/#dom-window-requestresize" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">Window.requestResize</code></a> method</li>
<li>The <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-4/#iframe-frame-sizing:~:text=If%20a-,%3Cmeta%20name%3Dresponsive%2Dembedded%2Dsizing%3E" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">&lt;meta name=responsive-embedded-sizing&gt;</code></a> meta tag</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds docs for all three features.</p>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

